# Shell scripts run on Linux, and a CRLF is not cosmetic there: `set -euo pipefail`
# is a syntax error that stops deploy.sh on its eleventh line.
#
# The committed blobs have always been LF. The CRs were added on the way OUT: `git
# archive` on Windows honours core.autocrlf, which Git for Windows sets to true in its
# system config, so a tree exported from this machine and unpacked on a box arrived with
# every shell script converted. CI never saw it -- its runners are Linux, where the same
# export is a no-op -- so this only appears when a deploy is driven from a workstation,
# which is exactly what an unavailable CI forces you to do.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the attribute win over the platform default in both directions,
# on checkout and on archive.
*.sh text eol=lf
